  "notes": "research/organ-references.md, 'Version 2' (2026-10-19): lymph_node v1's file with the v2 diagnostics' decisions (research/notebook-outputs/organ_v2_*). The generic 't cell' class is dropped: its specific sub-types are kept (the owner's rule, 2026-10-18). The split is v1's, carried through the atlas rows. Every class with at least 5 validation or test cells is in the suites, a short class giving what it has (cap_per_class); the suites' seeds are new. The calibration adds the chance floor (A3: committed 82 to 97 on the rare-class suite, coverage 91.1 to 88.2). The gene space, its sources, the identifier map, the missingness profiles, the modules' settings and the training are v1's. v1: research/organ-references.md, lymph node: Tabula Sapiens Lymph Node only. The class rule fails three classes with no kept Cell Ontology ancestor, dropped (70 cells): erythrocytes, plasmacytoid dendritic cells, hematopoietic precursor cells. The lineages are blood's (lymphoid, myeloid) plus stromal. The cells are immune like blood's, so the simulated uploads use blood's three real protein profiles computed over this gene space, not rank-transferred. The label audit (research/notebooks/organ_labels.py, 2026-10-18): the 'thymocytes' (181 cells, nearly all TSP7) express no thymocyte marker (CD1A, RAG1, DNTT 0%) and are mature T cells (CD3E 100%, TRAC 88%), so they are merged into CD4 T and CD8 T; the generic 'monocyte' class (766 cells) expresses CD14, FCN1 and LYZ in only 9 to 32% of cells and resembles T cells or endothelium in four of six donors, so it is dropped.",
